    {
      "featureId": "historic-england:nhle:1128585",
      "listEntry": "1128585",
      "name": "1, MARKET HILL",
      "designationType": "listed_building",
      "sourceUrl": "https://historicengland.org.uk/listing/the-list/list-entry/1128585?section=official-list-entry",
      "officialName": "1, MARKET HILL",
      "details": "Huntingdon MARKET HILL 1. ----------- 5140 No 1 TL 2371 2/201 II GV\n\n2. Early C19. Gault brick. 3 storeys, 3 windows, sashes with glazing bars over a modern bank frontage. Parapet. Low pitch roof not visible. Similar 3 window front to High Street. Important position and group value. (RCHM 34).\n\nListing NGR: TL2384871802"
    },
    {
      "featureId": "historic-england:nhle:1128608",
      "listEntry": "1128608",
      "name": "RAILINGS AND GATES OF NUMBER 71",
      "designationType": "listed_building",
      "sourceUrl": "https://historicengland.org.uk/listing/the-list/list-entry/1128608?section=official-list-entry",
      "officialName": "Railings and Gates of Number 71",
      "details": "Huntingdon HIGH STREET 1. 5140 (South-West Side) ----------------- Railings and gates of No 71 TL 2372 1/165 II GV\n\n2. C18 and later ironwork reset. Ornamental wrought iron railings on dwarf brick wall. Wrought-iron gates are C18 and are from elsewhere.\n\nListing NGR: TL2364172024"
    },
    {
      "featureId": "historic-england:nhle:1128651",
      "listEntry": "1128651",
      "name": "GATEHOUSE AND WALLS AT HINCHINGBROOKE HOUSE",
      "designationType": "listed_building",
      "sourceUrl": "https://historicengland.org.uk/listing/the-list/list-entry/1128651?section=official-list-entry",
      "officialName": "Gatehouse and Walls at Hinchingbrooke House",
      "details": "Huntingdon BRAMPTON ROAD 1. ------------- 5140 Gatehouse and walls at TL 27 SW 5/105 Hinchingbrooke House I GV\n\n2. C16 and earlier stone walls on either side of main entrance gate. The gatehouse is of circa 1500 and was brought by the Cromwells from Ramsey Abbey. Stone. Central carriage arch with pedestrian arches on either side, the right hand one is modern. The main arch has traceried spandrels with a quatrefoil frieze flanked by figures of wild men. Battlemented parapet. Pattern repeated on the internal face. High rubble walls on either side. (RCHM 10).\n\nListing NGR: TL2274471535"
    },
    {
      "featureId": "historic-england:nhle:1309881",
      "listEntry": "1309881",
      "name": "152, HIGH STREET",
      "designationType": "listed_building",
      "sourceUrl": "https://historicengland.org.uk/listing/the-list/list-entry/1309881?section=official-list-entry",
      "officialName": "152, HIGH STREET",
      "details": "Huntingdon HIGH STREET 1. 5140 (North-East Side) ---------------- No 152 (formerly listed as Clovelly) TL 2471 3/32 10.1.51. II GV\n\n2. Late C18. Stucco fronted with band at 2nd floor cill level. 3 storeys, 3 windows, C19 sashes, casements on top floor. Central doorway, fluted pilasters, pediment, fanlight. Roof not visible from street, but slated.\n\nListing NGR: TL2417071572"
    }
  ],
